# NVIDIA-Nemotron-Labs-3-Competitive-Coding-550B-A55B-NVFP4 across TWO Stations (TP2+EP2, FlashInfer TRT-LLM NVFP4 MoE, no offload) + code20
# Run 2026-10-08 23:13-23:49 PT. vLLM mp multi-node over one 400G RoCE link with the fabric block from
# recipes/fabric-data-direct (Data Direct overlay, tuner3.csv, NCCL_IB_TC=106). Rank 1 (right) started first.
# code20 ran on this boot after the bench: bench/code20.py, thinking on, T 1.0 / top_p 0.95, seed 1, max_tokens 24,000.
# Excerpt: lines selected verbatim from the raw files named below; hostnames, IPs, user names and GPU UUIDs
# replaced with <placeholders>. Nothing else edited. Times are Pacific (PT) unless the line says otherwise; vLLM server
# log lines are UTC ("10-09 03:05:11" = 2026-10-08 20:05:11 PDT).
# Bench: bench/bench-nemotron-ultra.sh (vllm bench serve, random 8,192 in / 1,024 out, ignore-eos, fresh seed per run,
# separate warm-up seed and shape). decode_agg = C x 1000 / mean TPOT. Prefix caching is OFF on the server, so the
# "hit 0.00% (0/0 tok) [prefix cache off]" field is 0 by construction (the /metrics delta is still taken per run).
# Power table: bench/power_windows.py over the 1 s nvidia-smi samples of both Stations (power-left.csv, power-right.csv);
# columns window, host, gpu, mean W, max W, samples. The RTX PRO 6000s are not used by this recipe; each held an unrelated,
# idle resident model during these runs (memory in use, idle power draw).


